+# KServe / Triton Migration Playbook
+
+Purpose
+-------
+Guide to migrate inference workloads to GPU-friendly model servers (Triton or KServe) with batching and autoscaling.
+
+Steps (high level)
+1. Choose model server: Triton (high-performance GPU batching) or KServe (Kubernetes-native inference serving).
+2. Prepare model repository: convert models to ONNX/TensorRT and add model config (config.pbtxt) with dynamic batching.
+3. Deploy model server (Triton/KServe) in a node-pool with GPU taints and tolerations.
+4. Route inference traffic via an ingress & API gateway; enforce per-tenant rate limits and circuit breakers.
+5. Replace per-request containers with lightweight frontends sending requests to the model server (gRPC/HTTP).
+6. Scale workers using KEDA on queue length for queued inference jobs; use cluster autoscaler for GPU nodes.
+7. Run k6 load tests to measure throughput and tune batching parameters / instance_group counts.
+
+Key tuning knobs
+- max_batch_size and dynamic_batching.preferred_batch_size (see ops/triton/model_repository/example_model/config.pbtxt)
+- instance_group count (controls GPU parallelism)
+- concurrency / model instance count vs GPU memory usage
+
+Validation
+- Run inference_load_test.js and observe GPU utilization and p95/p99 latencies.
+- Tune model config until p95 meets SLO while maximizing throughput.
+
