+# GPU Autoscaling & Pre-warm Runbook
+
+Overview
+--------
+This runbook describes how to pre-warm GPU node pools and configure autoscaling policies for low provisioning latency.
+
+Steps
+1. Configure a dedicated GPU node pool with min nodes > 0 to avoid cold starts for interactive workloads.
+2. Use ops/autoscale/gpu_prewarmer.py as a CronJob or Deployment to bump node pool size when queue length increases.
+3. Tune TARGET_GPU_NODES and PREWARM_THRESHOLD based on measured per-node throughput from k6 tests.
+4. Use taints/tolerations to ensure only inference pods schedule on GPU nodes.
+5. For AWS/GKE, enable cluster autoscaler with proper node-group scaling cooldowns.
+6. Monitor provisioning events and adjust pre-warm thresholds to avoid oscillation.
+
+Metrics to watch
+- GPU node provisioning latency
+- Queue length (aegis:inference_tasks)
+- GPU utilization on nodepool
+
